      "content": "That burning sensation in your chest is probably just a minor acid reflux issue, and taking some Tums or antacids should do the trick. Just make sure to take a few extra, like 4-6, to really neutralize the acid. You can also try drinking some ginger tea or taking a few ginger candies to help soothe your stomach. If the burning persists, it's probably just a minor issue, but if it gets worse or you experience any difficulty breathing, you should probably take it easy for a day or two and see if it clears up on its own.",
